### What is an Operating System?
> Interface between Hardware and Software 
Software - no touch and feel but can experience it 
Hardware - Touch and feel
Examples of OS:- Windows, LINUX, UNIX, ios, android

Basic Functions of OS:-
1. Memory management
2. File Management
3. I/O Management
4. Process Management
5. Security Management

Tenancy - Multiple user can use it at the same time 

1. In the Linux we are running a Program so the Linux is installed in the hardware 
2. First we need to know where am I currently 
  1. pwd - print working directory 
  2. ls - list of directories 
(**ll is a shortcut for ls -la**)
3. ls -l -a(when we use -a we get all the files including the hidden files)
4. . - is the current directory
5. .. - is the previous directory 
6. mkdir - create directory
    - for using already created path we need to use mkdir -p <path>
7. man
8. watch
9. cat - content of the file will be visible or if we what to concatinate 
10. tail
11. more/less
12. head
13. touch - it creates and also updates the timestamp
14. chmod
15. grep
16. mv - it moves and also renames the files
17. awk - printing out values of only one file 
18. free -h - for human readable 
        -m in mega 
(please explain the output of free command)-interview question
19. vim or vi - vi is the older version, new is vim 
